       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4250 mg three times daily, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** the usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is about 5 times that.\n- **Risk:** a dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIt may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n\n- **850 mg** three times daily (2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release)\n- **425 mg** three times daily (this isn't a standard tablet strength)\n- **500 mg** three times daily (1,500 mg/day)\n\nIf you're starting metformin, the usual approach is 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, then titrating up every 1\u20132 weeks as tolerated. Please check the intended dose with your resident or attending. Once you confirm it, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
